## Lore

Savage Lummox are the giants of the Haven Mutants: eight to ten feet of
muscle, strong enough to stand in for a comic-book brute, and not very bright.
About half have human faces; the rest have long, horse-like skulls with big
fangs, on necks that are either several times normal length or short and as
thick as a stump. Though their hides are M.D.C. and their strength is
supernatural, they bury themselves in homemade armor pieced from scrap and
decorated with spikes, horns, fins, paint and crab-like spines of hardened
resin. The loose, clattering suits can be heard a long way off. They glue it
all together with a resin they ooze from their mouths, since none of them can
work a tool.

Lummox solve problems by force or the threat of it. They believe everything
the Shamans teach, including that the mutants are a chosen people blessed by
the Mighty Lady, and they are fiercely loyal to all Haven Mutants. They watch
outsiders from a distance and follow the lead of cleverer mutants, but anyone
who damages a sacred place or a mutant home, or threatens a mutant, gets a
savage beating.

They cannot read, speak a rough broken slang, and are easy to fool, yet they
know their own limits, laugh off insults about their wits, and fear nothing:
not monsters, not magic, not psychics, not robots. They see themselves as the
guardians of the mutant people, often protect human and D-Bee women and
children, and get on well with the Knights of the White Rose, beside whom they
have fought many times. They use every kind of melee weapon, heavy guns and
energy weapons, and can hurl energy bolts from their hands.

## Mutant Shaman

Any sizable clan is led by a Shaman, who keeps the race''s attributes and
abilities and gains the bonuses the `shaman` variant carries: +2 I.Q., +1D4+2
M.A., and +3D6+10 P.P.E. at the start. **The Shaman also gains 1D6 P.P.E.
per level on top of this race''s own 1D10 per level; add it by hand.**

The Shaman''s skills (Animal Husbandry, Literacy in American, Medicinal
Brewing, Dance, Fasting, both Histories, Holistic Medicine, Public Speaking,
Sing and Veterinary Science) are added by the variant. **In the book they
REPLACE every Secondary skill, every Piloting skill and every modern W.P.** A
Shaman never uses a modern weapon, vehicle or machine. The app cannot remove
skills through a variant, so the player and G.M. drop those picks by hand.

A Shaman advances on the **Gateway Knight & Mutant Shaman** ladder (printed
79), not the Haven Mutant one: 0, 2,351, 4,701, 9,401, 18,801, 28,001, 38,001,
53,001, 77,001, 102,001, 143,001, 195,201, 240,401, 310,601, 360,801.

Shamans are also the clan''s lawgivers, judges and chiefs, and they can pray to
Isis, the Mighty Lady:

- **Prayer of Strength**: 01-20%, +5% per level, to be heard. Grants +6 P.S.,
  +1D4x10 M.D.C., and 48 hours without food or water with no ill effect. Up to
  six times a year.
- **Prayer of Inspiration or Wisdom**: 01-12%, +3% per level (+10% after a
  week of fasting). If Isis hears, a dream brings insight, an idea or a warning
  about the matter prayed on.

## Starting Equipment

A large Bone Club and a Bone Dagger, one weapon per W.P. with 1D6+3 extra
E-Clips or ammo clips per modern weapon, 2D4 days of food and water, homemade
body armor, a utility belt, a backpack, a satchel or big sack, a pair of
waterskins, a wooden cross, 12 wooden stakes, 50 feet of rope, six iron
spikes, binoculars and personal items.

## GM Notes

Alignments run mostly Scrupulous (35%), Unprincipled (30%) or Anarchist (20%),
with 15% other. They use strength to intimidate and keep the peace, and are the
Shamans'' most loyal backers. Size 8 to 10 feet, 500 to 800 lbs. They could
live to 90, but violence brings the average down to 2D6+45 years; females are
every bit as tough as males. NPCs average level 1D4+2.

They are fond of the White Rose''s Knights and Squires and of the Garden folk,
though they may hide it around Mantis Men and Leopard Men. They trade with other
mutants, the Garden, Horune Pirates and other pirates without trusting them;
have no love for barbarians, Horune Pirates or Splugorth''s Minions but trade
with them anyway; and count intruders, slavers, madmen, ghosts, monsters,
Undead Horrors and magical creatures as foes. They live in caves, basements and tunnels among
the ruins, on Jersey Side as well as in Madhaven.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'savage-lummox');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
